{"id": "EUVD-2026-97711", "enisaUuid": "846409b7-c913-3d03-a8e1-e3ae1422f30a", "description": "ImageMagick before 6.9.13-57 and 7.x before 7.1.2-32 contains a stack overflow in the MSL decoder caused by an incorrect depth check that fails to limit recursion. Attackers can supply a set of crafted MSL images that exhaust the stack when one of them is read, crashing the process and causing a denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T02:33:58", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-462x-739v-qvq2", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/507aee2308046b25e251d0be1a5371327bb79683", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/c10823904b251d07fe79346a7136b0af295d451b", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-6.9.13-57-and-7-x-before-7.1.2-32-stack-overflow-in-msl-decoder"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m4x9-m38x-9jc8", "CVE-2026-109267"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4196dfed-ad1f-3d07-8a54-e5332638a358", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}, {"id": "bd07c848-3eb9-3525-8c82-ed43df6eb587", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7a877d0f-e1f9-3b37-bb61-f8f59d552bf5", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}